'''Kwangju''' ({{Langx|ko|상태}}), officialy the '''Republic of Kwangju''' ({{Langx|ko|광주 공화국|Kwangju Konghwaguk}}) is a [[W:Unitary state|unitary]] [[W:Parliamentary republic|parliamentary republic]] located in [[East Fosia]], sharing a land border with [[Morsco]] to the east, and maritime borders with [[Zong]] to the south and [[Okaiken]] to the east. In the 2025 census, Kwangju recorded a population of nearly 83 million people, distributed across a total area of {{Convert|213,829|sqkm|sqmi}}. The capital and most populous city in Kwangju is [[Jinju]], which is also one of the [[List of largest cities|world's largest cities]].

Archaeological evidence indicates that Kwangju has been inhabited as early as 10,000 BC. According to founding legends, [[Geunchogo]], a descendant of heaven, founded Haemosu in 2326 BC, with it's capital at Mundeok <small>(present day Chaegok)</small>. Following the fall of Haemosu to the Zong Pcing Dynasty, which installed the Jiasan Commandery on the peninsula, leaving many smaller kingdoms on the southern part of the peninsula. The largest of these, Kwanŭmdong drove out the Zong from the west in 320 AD, becoming the dominant force on the Kwangju Peninsula for the rest of its history. The remaining two kingdoms, [[Bamgogae]] and [[Tangsŏn]] remained constantly at odds with [[Kwanŭmdong]] over control of the peninsula. The three kingdoms were unified in 1901, under [[Emperor Wŏnsingi]], establishing the [[Kwangju Empire]]. The empire lasted until 1917, when it was annexed into the [[Mitoyagi Empire]] following the coerced [[Kwangju-Sanese Annexation Treaty]]. Near the end of the [[Great Adonian War]], Kwangju was liberated from Mitoyagi in February 1952 and was subsequently occupied by Allied forces until the end of the war. Differences on how to govern Kwangju resulted in its partitioning, creating the [[People's Republic of Kwangju]] (PRK) and the [[Republic of Howan]]. [[Kwangju reunification]] occurred on 23 April 2013.  

Kwangju has Adonia's [[List of countries by GDP (PPP)|sixth-largest economy by GDP (PPP)]], and is sixth-largest economy by nominal measures. It is also Fosia's fourth-largest economy, driven by its exports of [[W:Rare earth metals|rare earth metals]], electronics, robotics, shipbuilding, and automobiles. Kwangju is a member of the [[Adonian Community]], the G20, the [[South Cilician Mutual Assistance Treaty]], and is a founding member of the [[East Fosian Sphere]]. 

==Etymology== 
The name ''Kwangju'' (Kwangeo: 광주; Hanja: 光州) is of Sino-Kwangjunese origin, translating literally to "State of Light" or "Province of Splendor." The name is a compound of two characters:

* '''Kwang''' (광, ''gwang''), meaning "light," "brightness," or "luster."
* '''Ju''' (주, ''ju''), meaning "province," "state," or "prefecture."

Historically, the name originally referred only to the royal capital region located in the fertile southern basin. In the post-dynastic era, the name underwent a process of ''[[W:Pars pro toto|pars pro toto]]'' (where a part stands for the whole), eventually becoming the exonym for the entire peninsula.

The spelling ''Kwangju'' follows the older [[W:McCune–Reischauer romanization|McCune–Reischauer romanization system]] (which favors the hard ''K''), distinguishing it from the revised romanization ''Gwangju'' often used in modern diplomatic contexts.

