===Political parties and elections===
Post-reunification, Kwangju has developed a vibrant [[W:Multi-party system|multi-party system]], with political parties representing the entirety of the [[W:Political spectrum|political spectrum]]. However, with unification of Kwangju, the nation quickly became divided between two political parties. These parties, [[Minjoo Party of Kwangju|the Minjoo Party]], and the [[Justice Party (Kwangju)|Justice Party]], also known as ''Jeongui''. The Minjoo Party is currently in power in Kwangju, holding the position of Prime Minster, and a majority in the National Assembly (193 out of 300 seats). There are no communist parties in Kwangju, due to the criminalizing of "Far-left politics" in 2012.

Current parties in Kwangju include:
*[[Minjoo Party of Kwangju|Minjoo Party]] (centre-left)
*[[Justice Party (Kwangju)|Jeongui]] (centre-right)
*[[People's Party (Andalus)|People's Party]] (right)
*[[Kwangju Labour Party|Labour Party]] (centre-left)
*[[Grand National Party (Kwangju)|Grand National Party]] (centre)
*[[Green Party of Kwangju|Green Party]] (left)

