===Language===
Kwangju is the national language of Kwangju. However due to heavy influence from western Fosia and Lurandia, Mercian is commonly heard throughout Kwangju, and is recongized as the main "business language of Kwangju". Most signs in Kwangju are in both Kwangju and Avelian, as Avelian has become the 2nd most common language in Kwangju.

Sanese has been recognized as a national language, and holds official status in the former territory of the Republic of Seongpo, where almost a quarter of the population speaks Sanese as their mother tongue. There has been a concerted effort to preserve the Sanese speaking-culture, as it has come under increasing pressure to assimilate into the Kwangju-speaking sphere.
===Religion===
Religion in Kwangju saw a rapid decline during the prolonged division of Kwangju. Kwangju is a [[wikipedia:Secular state|secular state]], as the constitution of Kwangju protects the freedom of religion, and bans the designation of an official state religion. As of 2013, the majortiy of Kwangju (53.8%) identify themselves as   [[wikipedia:Irreligion|irreligious]], while 23% identify themselves as Christian, 22.1% as Buddhist, and 1.1% as Other. The majority of Kwangju (67%) say religion has no important role in their daily lives.

